@startuml
title ORE configuration: the reporting half
hide empty members
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
left to right direction

package "ores.reporting" #E8F4FF {
  class report_definition {
    id : uuid
    name : text
    report_type_id : uuid
    party_id : uuid
    schedule_expression : text
    concurrency_policy : text
    fsm_state_id : uuid
    scheduler_job_id : uuid
    workspace_id : uuid
  }
  class report_type {
    id : uuid
    code : text
    name : text
  }
  class report_configuration {
    report_definition_id : uuid
    configuration_type_id : uuid
    configuration_id : uuid
  }
  class configuration_type {
    id : uuid
    code : text
    name : text
    owning_component : text
    parameterised : boolean
  }
  class configuration {
    id : uuid
    name : text
    configuration_type_id : uuid
    party_id : uuid
    workspace_id : uuid
  }
  class configuration_parameter {
    configuration_id : uuid
    parameter_definition_id : uuid
    position : integer
    value : text
  }
  class parameter_definition {
    id : uuid
    configuration_type_id : uuid
    scope : text
    subtype : text
    name : text
    value_domain_id : uuid
    required : boolean
    position : integer
  }
  class value_domain {
    id : uuid
    code : text
    storage_type : text
    referenced_entity : text
  }

report_definition *-- "1" report_type : typed as
report_definition *-- "0..*" report_configuration : binds
report_configuration *-- "1" configuration_type : by type
report_configuration *-- "1" configuration : to
configuration *-- "1" configuration_type : is one of
configuration *-- "0..*" configuration_parameter : holds
configuration_parameter *-- "1" parameter_definition : named by
parameter_definition *-- "1" value_domain : valued as
parameter_definition *-- "1" configuration_type : belongs to

note right of report_definition
  a scheduled report: what to run, when, and under which concurrency policy. Report types are ours, not ORE's.
end note
note right of report_configuration
  the report's slots. One row per configuration type it binds: the type is the slot, configuration_id fills it. Several reports may fill the same slot with the same configuration.
end note
note right of configuration_type
  the kinds of configuration a report can bind: Stress Testing, Simulation, Sensitivity, SIMM Calibration, Historical Return, Basel Traffic Light, Credit Simulation, and the ORE run itself.
end note
note right of configuration
  one named, reusable configuration. The name is ours; the detail lives with the component named by owning_component.
end note
note right of configuration_parameter
  one value. value is text because the domain says what it is; the mapper writes it into the document.
end note
note right of parameter_definition
  the vocabulary of an ORE run document: which parameter names a scope and subtype accepts, and the domain of each value. 165 of the 218 names observed belong to exactly one analytic kind.
end note
note right of value_domain
  what a value is - currency, date, boolean, integer, tenor, document, list - and, where it names something, the entity it refers to.
end note
note as rule_0
  Every discriminator column is an FK to a seeded lookup, not a text code. A note listing valid values is a lookup that has not been built yet.
end note
note as rule_1
  A correlation is pairwise by its meaning: two asset classes and an index within each. A matrix is many such rows, not a wider struct.
end note
note as rule_2
  A value indexed by factor - a loading, a weight per bucket - is a row per (owner, factor); a relation among participants is a row per participant.
end note
note as rule_3
  The ORE XML structure is rebuilt by the mappers in ores.ore. The model holds domain entities and nothing about how they are written down.
end note

@enduml
